I take my laptop.
I show them my new room.
"This is my room," I say.
"Your room is very good, Maya," mother says.
Sofia is standing near her mother.
"Where is the bed?" she asks.
"This is my bed," I say.
"There is a table there too."
Diego looks at the screen.
Lola is in his arms.
"Who else is in your room?" he asks.
"There is no one else here, brother," I say.
I turn the laptop towards the window.
I show them the view outside.
There is bright sunlight outside.
"It is very sunny there," father says.
"Yes, this is a beautiful day in Kochi," I say.
"But it is night at your place now."
There is great happiness on their faces.
